* $KEY treats the string stored in KEY as the name of the variable to read.
* Angle brackets index ARRAY by position and TABLE by keys such as 'Lean'.
* DEFINE binds GREET to its labeled entry point. RETURN yields the value assigned to GREET.
    WORD = 'Lean'
    KEY = 'WORD'
    OUTPUT = $KEY

    A = ARRAY(2)
    A<1> = 'red'
    A<2> = 'blue'
    OUTPUT = A<1> ' | ' A<2>

    H = TABLE()
    H<'Lean'> = 9
    H<'Zuriel'> = 7
    OUTPUT = 'Lean:' H<'Lean'> ' | Zuriel:' H<'Zuriel'>

    DEFINE('GREET(X)')
    OUTPUT = GREET(WORD) :(END)
GREET GREET = 'Hi ' X :(RETURN)
END
